Is there a public Roslyn API that tells me which property or method a union pattern calls?

For example, how can I get the `Choice.Value` symbol for `choice is int` here?

```csharp
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;

[Union]
public struct Choice
{
    public Choice(int value) => Value = value;
    public object Value { get; }
}

public static class Consumer
{
    public static bool Match(Choice choice) => choice is int;
    public static bool Explicit(Choice choice) => choice.Value is int;
}
```

`GetOperation` gives me an `IPropertyReferenceOperation` for the explicit `choice.Value` access. For `choice is int`, I only get:

```text
IsPattern
  ParameterReference
  TypePattern
```

I couldn't find the property reference in the control-flow graph either. For unions with `TryGetValue` or `HasValue`, I'd also need to know which member was selected. Is there something similar to `IListPatternOperation.IndexerSymbol` for this?

